From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:39:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 182/342] meson_vdec: forget hand-backs from before the
 firmware got its frames

With its frames (the answer to its command 1), the H.264 firmware takes all
of them as free. Frames given back before that, still in the driver's queue
or in its two places (AV_SCRATCH_7/8), were taken back once more later, when
they could hold new pictures the reader had: after a size change, one frame
showed the picture of a later one. The setup now drops them. The KDL dump
names HEVC sessions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp       | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp
index cb19cd193c..15907a83d7 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/video/meson_vdec/meson_vdec.cpp
@@ -1038,6 +1038,13 @@ MesonVdec::_SetupH264Frames(const uint32* info)
 	fHeight = 16 * mbHeight - cropBottom;
 	fBytesPerRow = bytesPerRow;
 	fLumaSize = lumaSize;
+	// With its frames, the firmware takes all of them as free: frames given
+	// back before (still queued, or in its two places) would be taken back
+	// again later, when they may hold new pictures the reader has.
+	fBackHead = 0;
+	fBackCount = 0;
+	_SetDos(AV_SCRATCH_7, 0);
+	_SetDos(AV_SCRATCH_8, 0);
 	_SetDos(AV_SCRATCH_1, fMotionVectors.physical);
 	_SetDos(AV_SCRATCH_4, fMotionVectors.physical + motionVectors);
 	_SetDos(AV_SCRATCH_0, (maxReferences << 24) | (count << 16)
@@ -1597,7 +1604,7 @@ MesonVdec::Dump()
 	kprintf("meson_vdec: %s %s, %" B_PRIu32 "x%" B_PRIu32 ", %" B_PRIu32
 		" frames, %" B_PRIu32 " decoded, %" B_PRIu32 " skipped, queue %"
 		B_PRIu32 ", held %#" B_PRIx32 "%s%s%s\n",
-		fCodec == MESON_VDEC_H264 ? "H.264" : "MPEG-1/2",
+		fCodec == MESON_VDEC_H264 ? "H.264" : _IsHevc() ? "HEVC" : "MPEG-1/2",
 		fRunning ? "running" : "stopped", fWidth, fHeight, fFrameCount,
 		fFramesDecoded, fFramesSkipped, fQueueCount, fHeld,
 		fFatal ? ", fatal error" : "",
